From: Ayoub Zaki <ayoub.zaki@embetrix.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spl: print the loaded i.MX container software version

Print the version from the container header after its images load
successfully. Use the authenticated header when AHAB is enabled.
Normal console handling keeps the message silent in the prod profile.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [boot diagnostics]
Signed-off-by: Ayoub Zaki <ayoub.zaki@embetrix.com>
---
 common/spl/spl_imx_container.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/spl/spl_imx_container.c b/common/spl/spl_imx_container.c
--- a/common/spl/spl_imx_container.c
+++ b/common/spl/spl_imx_container.c
@@ -213,6 +213,9 @@ static int read_auth_container(struct spl_image_info *spl_image,
 		}
 	}
 
+	printf("Boot container software version: %u\n",
+	       (unsigned int)authhdr->sw_version);
+
 #if defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD) && defined(CONFIG_IMX_TRUSTY_OS)
 	/* Everything checks out, get the sw_version now. */
 	spl_image->rbindex = (uint64_t)container->sw_version;
